diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..7ecec94 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -46,6 +46,30 @@ This will ask for your 1password authorization to read and set the environment v
 * [Staging](https://dashboard.stripe.com/acct_1SdTbuRvb8txnPBR/test/dashboard)
 * [Production](https://dashboard.stripe.com/acct_1SNy97RwChFE4it8/dashboard)
 
+## Plans
+
+Hosted Fizzy is going paid:
+
+| Plan        | Price     | Cards     | Storage |
+| ----------- | --------- | --------- | ------- |
+| Free        | Free      | 1,000     | 1 GB    |
+| Unlimited   | $20/month | Unlimited | 5 GB    |
+| Unlimited+  | $25/month | Unlimited | 500 GB  |
+
+The plans live in `Account::Subscription::Plan`. Stripe hosts both checkout and
+the customer portal, and reports subscription changes to `POST /stripe/webhooks`,
+which is authenticated with `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`. Each plan is priced with its
+own Stripe price, configured through `STRIPE_UNLIMITED_PRICE_ID` and
+`STRIPE_UNLIMITED_PLUS_PRICE_ID`.
+
+A free account that ran out of cards can still draft, but publishing and creating
+through the API are refused, and its admins are pitched an upgrade from the account
+settings.
+
+Support tools live in the admin area: `/admin/accounts` lists the accounts and each
+name opens its page, where an account can be comped (`Comp` / `Uncomp`) and have its
+card count and bytes used overridden (`Override` / `Reset`).
+
 ## Working with Push Notifications
 
 To test native push notifications (APNs and FCM) locally, start the dev server with the `--push` flag:
